# Melite deployment environment — copy to .env (gitignored) and fill
# for YOUR machine. Every value is optional; scripts fall back to
# neutral localhost/$HOME defaults so a fresh clone runs without one.
# Never commit real values (hosts, units, weights roots) — the tree
# stays deployment-neutral.

# ── the lane (scripts/lane-*.sh, ship-lane.sh) ──
# Where the dsh-dev profile tree lives (lane-rebuild's target; lane-sync
# takes --dsh-home — no-env law, 2026-11-16).
#LANE_DSH_HOME=$HOME/.dsh-dev
# ship-lane's unit+origin are FLAGS (no-env law, 2026-11-16): --unit /
# --origin name the sanctioned lane TOGETHER (one alone is refused); to
# move the sanctioned lane itself, edit the two defaults in the script.
# Host shown in lane-rebuild's URL hint when not localhost: a FLAG now
# (no-env law, 2026-11-16): --public-host HOST.

# ── promote-prod.sh ──
# Lane URLs are FLAGS (no-env law, 2026-11-16): --prod-url / --dev-url.
# The only env that script reads is DSH_PROD_TOKEN (secret, env-or-file).

# ── e2e GPU lanes ──
# The ComfyUI weights tree (e2e-h3-gpu-lane.sh) is a FLAG now (no-env
# law, 2026-11-16): --weights-root PATH. The gpu/studio lane launchers
# take their dsh binary as --dsh-bin BIN.

# ── engine probes (tools/reproject-combos.mjs, regen-node-vocab.mjs) ──
#MELITE_OBJECT_INFO=http://127.0.0.1:8188/object_info
